dental implants.\n\nWhat is a dental implant? Shaped like a screw, it is a durable post that is surgically placed into the upper or lower jaw. Once in place, a dental implant fuses with the bone over a period of several months. Essentially, the implant becomes a part of the jaw. But people who receive implants do not need to wait for months to restore their smiles. Instead, they can rejuvenate their appearance and regain some functionality immediately.\n\n\n## The “Magic” (Science, Really) Of All-On-4 Dental Implants In Los Angeles, CA\n\n\nAs alluded to, a highly trained dentist can place implants and then use them as a foundation to permanently secure a set of replacement teeth. The replacement teeth stay in place and can absorb practically all the chewing and biting forces that normal teeth can.\n\nAt the practice in Los Angeles, CA, the TeethToday® system is followed. Directly after placing dental implants, a dentist affixes a temporary set of replacement teeth made from nanoceramic materials to the dental implant posts. The outcome is an instant smile that looks very natural.\n\nAfter several months, the temporary teeth will be replaced with a full-arch prosthesis made of zirconia.\n\n\n## Will Anyone Notice All-On-4 Dental Implants?\n\n\nThe before-after transformation for people who receive All-On-4 permanent full mouth dental implants is nothing short of dramatic. Accordingly, if a patient and their dentist feel that All-On-4 dental implants are the right choice, then expect that people will notice the difference. This is positive, though! Many people are thrilled by how much more confidence they have, especially after getting compliments on the way they look after an All-On-4 treatment.\n\n\n## Starting The All-On-4 Dental Implant Process In Los Angeles, CA\n\n\nDoes it seem like All-On-4 dental implants could be the right decision for your needs? Even if other dentists have told you that you cannot receive dental implants, we invite you to make a consultation with West LA Implants. Implant and cosmetic dentist Dr. Tony Barriere has a passion for bringing the latest treatments to his patients in the Los Angeles area, including All-on-4 dental implants.\n\nSchedule an appointment Dr. Tony Barriere in our office by Los Angeles, CA to schedule an appointment today!\n\nPrevPreviousThe Best Ways To Find Affordable Dental Implants!\n\nNextWhen Is Dental Implant Surgery Needed?Next\n\n\n#### More To Explore\n\n\n\n### Are There Factors That Determine Which Type Of Dental Implant Procedure I Can Get Treated With?\n\n\nDental implants in Los Angeles, FL, are a safe and effective way to replace missing or damaged teeth. They are\n\nRead More »\n\nAugust 20, 2023\n\n\n### Does Anything Happen To My Jawbone If I Don’t Immediately Replace My Missing Teeth With Dental Implants?\n\n\nDental implants in Los Angeles, FL, are a gold standard tooth replacement option that are surgically placed in a patient’s\n\nAugust 14, 2023\n\n\n## You Are Welcome Here.\n\n\nSchedule your consultation today.\n\nCall Now\n\nFacebook Instagram Youtube Yelp Google\n\n\n#### Contact Us\n\n\nAddress:\n\n12301 Wilshire Blvd Suite 205,\n\nLos Angeles, CA 90025\n\n(310) 481-0111\n\n\n#### Hours\n\n\nMonday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nTuesday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nWednesday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nThursday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nFriday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nSaturday: Closed\n\nSunday: Closed\n\n\n#### Services\n\n\n\n#### About Us\n\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nDental Website by Progressive Dental Marketing",
